1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,506
Getting started with PestBase: From signing in to getting paid, in a few minutes

2
00:00:04,556 --> 00:00:07,915
Go to your PestBase address and type the email address your administrator added for you.

3
00:00:07,965 --> 00:00:10,725
Choose "Email me a sign-in link". There is no password to remember.

4
00:00:10,775 --> 00:00:14,697
Open the link in the email, or type the six-digit code it contains.

5
00:00:14,747 --> 00:00:20,101
Today is your starting point: what needs attention, today's jobs and the money coming in.

6
00:00:20,151 --> 00:00:28,150
Choose any card to jump straight to that list.

7
00:00:28,200 --> 00:00:32,495
Customers: Add the people and sites you work for

8
00:00:32,545 --> 00:00:38,726
Customers lists everyone you work for. Search by name, postcode or phone.

9
00:00:38,776 --> 00:00:49,305
Add a new customer: name, contact details and the site address.

10
00:00:49,355 --> 00:00:52,211
Then choose "Create customer".

11
00:00:52,261 --> 00:00:56,414
The customer's page keeps their quotes, jobs, reports and invoices together.

12
00:00:56,464 --> 00:00:59,474
Quotes: Price the work and send it for approval

13
00:00:59,524 --> 00:01:02,578
Start a quote straight from the customer's page.

14
00:01:02,628 --> 00:01:13,686
Add a line for each piece of work: pest, service, quantity and price.

15
00:01:13,736 --> 00:01:18,404
Totals, including VAT, update as you type.

16
00:01:18,454 --> 00:01:20,319
Choose "Send quote" to email it to the customer as a PDF.

17
00:01:20,369 --> 00:01:26,591
Check the message, then send it.

18
00:01:26,641 --> 00:01:29,007
When the customer says yes, mark the quote as accepted.

19
00:01:29,057 --> 00:01:32,065
Jobs: Book the work and give it to a technician

20
00:01:32,115 --> 00:01:34,084
An accepted quote can be booked as a job in one step.

21
00:01:34,134 --> 00:01:41,232
Add who to meet on site, when, and which technician is going.

22
00:01:41,282 --> 00:01:46,259
Regular contracts can repeat weekly, monthly or quarterly.

23
00:01:46,309 --> 00:01:51,364
The technician is told about the job straight away, in PestBase and by email.

24
00:01:51,414 --> 00:01:55,589
Once the customer has agreed the time, choose "Confirm".

25
00:01:55,639 --> 00:01:59,155
Jobs lists every visit. Switch to the calendar to see the week at a glance.

26
00:02:01,270 --> 00:02:05,380
Inspection reports: Technicians fill them in on site, on their phone

27
00:02:05,430 --> 00:02:10,486
On site, open PestBase in your phone's browser. Today lists your visits in order.

28
00:02:10,536 --> 00:02:12,212
Choose "Start job" when you arrive.

29
00:02:12,262 --> 00:02:16,716
The inspection report opens, ready to fill in from top to bottom.

30
00:02:16,766 --> 00:02:21,102
Record the visit type and the level of pest activity.

31
00:02:21,152 --> 00:02:35,166
Describe what you found, then add a finding for each area.

32
00:02:35,216 --> 00:02:40,221
Add photos straight from the phone's camera.

33
00:02:40,271 --> 00:02:50,411
Note what you did and every product used, for your records and the customer's.

34
00:02:50,461 --> 00:02:57,138
Finally, you and the customer sign on the screen.

35
00:02:57,188 --> 00:03:02,668
Choose "Complete job". The report goes to the office and an invoice is raised.

36
00:03:05,800 --> 00:03:08,712
Reports: Check the technician's report and send it to the customer

37
00:03:08,762 --> 00:03:12,999
Back in the office, Today shows the report is in and ready to check.

38
00:03:13,049 --> 00:03:22,285
The completed report has everything the technician recorded, with photos and signatures.

39
00:03:22,335 --> 00:03:28,167
Choose "Email report" to send it to the customer as a PDF.

40
00:03:28,217 --> 00:03:31,227
Invoices: Get paid for the work

41
00:03:31,277 --> 00:03:35,363
Completing the job raised a draft invoice from the quoted price.

42
00:03:35,413 --> 00:03:41,323
Check it, then choose "Send invoice". It goes by email with the PDF attached.

43
00:03:41,373 --> 00:03:50,399
When money arrives, choose "Record payment". Part payments are fine.

44
00:03:50,449 --> 00:03:56,585
The invoice shows what has been paid and what is still owed.

45
00:03:56,635 --> 00:04:01,990
Invoices lists everything you have billed. PestBase reminds you when payments are due or overdue.

46
00:04:02,040 --> 00:04:09,628
Need a hand?: Open Guide from the menu for step-by-step help with screenshots

47
00:04:09,678 --> 00:04:13,200
PestBase: Every job, from first quote to paid invoice. pestbase.co.uk

